  "narrative": "This synthesis closes the current follow-up wave and clarifies what is supported. The strongest within-dataset evidence remains a compact measured-association panel: feature_002 and feature_010 are associated with less-negative composite dependency scores, whereas feature_037 and feature_063 are associated with more-negative scores, i.e. stronger dependency. The main effect for feature_002 is +0.832 [0.766, 0.897] in the claimed less-negative direction (H47/R23); for feature_010 it is +0.423 [0.327, 0.520] (H25/R40); for feature_037 it is +0.833 [0.767, 0.898] in the claimed stronger-dependency direction (H30/R42); and for feature_063 it is +0.227 [0.131, 0.323] (H44/R45), with independent validation at +0.290 [0.143, 0.437] (R52). The feature_063 conditional when feature_037=0 was also validated at +0.269 [0.128, 0.410] (H83/R57 and R65). The accepted conditional claims for feature_002, feature_010, feature_037, and feature_063 should be interpreted as persistence or stability checks on this correlated panel, not as many separate predictors or as causal independence. New validation and response-deadline evidence does not extend the supported panel. H5 (feature_058 claimed stronger-dependency association) remains unsupported: discovery +0.021 [-0.039, 0.080] and stringent validation +0.035 [-0.052, 0.121], both far below the 0.15-unit threshold and compatible with no difference. H91 (feature_010 interaction when feature_002=1) was +0.210 [0.019, 0.400] in discovery but +0.181 [-0.120, 0.482] under stringent validation; the direction is suggestive but the evidence is too imprecise and the discovery interval did not establish threshold magnitude, so the threshold-level interaction claim remains rejected. H62 (feature_031 among feature_002=0) gives discovery +0.094 [0.024, 0.163] and validation -0.005 [-0.102, 0.093]; the independent null and subthreshold point estimate justify rejection. H122 (feature_003 among cells with all four accepted panel members zero) gives discovery +0.164 [0.101, 0.228] and validation +0.100 [0.010, 0.191]. The independent result confirms positive direction but is clearly below the threshold, and combined evidence supports only a small association, not a scientifically meaningful difference; therefore I reject the threshold-level claim and close it. Negative findings remain broad: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_024, feature_041, feature_048, feature_023, feature_035, feature_060, feature_033, feature_001, feature_053, feature_054, feature_046 level contrasts tested, feature_052 level contrast, feature_061 level contrast, feature_034 tested contrasts, feature_044-type signature comparisons when analytically testable, and many interaction probes do not support threshold-level claims. The standardized signature claims H1-H3 are analytically invalid because exact comparison levels were not populated and should not be treated as negative scientific results. Unresolved uncertainty remains mostly in low-prevalence binary screens still awaiting analysis, sparse high-log-PFS feature_063 strata where H108 improves interpretability but does not fully resolve the sparse high-log-PFS estimate, and possible subthreshold feature_003 associations. The most informative next analysis is the newly registered interaction test for feature_010 within feature_063=1, because the reciprocal conditional means suggest a potentially enhanced feature_010 less-negative association in the feature_063-positive stratum; this is a focused interaction follow-up rather than another correlated mean-difference conditional. In parallel, existing broad binary screens should be run modestly to avoid missing any additional predictor, but further conditional proliferation on the accepted panel is low value. All conclusions are limited to measured associations in the supplied dataset; they do not establish causality, mechanism, biological role, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 synthesize. Validation outcomes: H91 and H5 remain rejected; H62 rejected; H122 rejected as threshold-level claim despite direction replication but validation magnitude below 0.15. Supported within-dataset panel: feature_002 less-negative, feature_010 less-negative, feature_037 stronger dependency, feature_063 stronger dependency. Main feature_063 validated and feature_063 conditional feature_037=0 validated. Accepted conditional claims are correlated stability checks, not independent predictors. Negative broad set includes research markers feature_007/058/015, feature_031 conditional, feature_003 threshold claim, many categorical contrasts, and unsupported interactions. Unresolved: low-prevalence active screens, sparse high-log-PFS feature_063 stratum, possible subthreshold feature_003 effect. Next registered analysis: feature_010 interaction by feature_063=1 direction +1; continue modest broad screens and avoid further correlated conditional claims. Future validation, if needed, should prioritize either an important unresolved threshold claim or a new strong candidate rather than accepted correlated conditionals."
}
